not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"The Rack","oracle_id":"3d873e1d-4fac-42c4-bb31-77e76099e1ef","oracle_text":"As this artifact enters, choose an opponent.\nAt the beginning of the chosen player's upkeep, this artifact deals X damage to that player, where X is 3 minus the number of cards in their hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2006-10-06","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it.","oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It will trigger \"enters\" abilities and \"leaves the battlefield\" abilities. Note that the card does not go to the graveyard, so it will not trigger \"goes to the graveyard\" abilities.","oracle_id":"19ea326f-45ff-4bc0-a957-7d3f22dd8c6f","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This could be used to make the target of another spell or ability illegal if this wasn't a sorcery (which makes it really hard to do that). This is because the Flickered permanent leaves the battlefield and then returns as a completely different permanent, and the targeted spell will not recognize it.","oracle_id":"19ea326f-45ff-4bc0-a957-7d3f22dd8c6f","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This spell effectively \"resets\" the permanent to being just like it was freshly cast. All counters, Auras, effects, and so on are removed when it is exiled. Then it comes back onto the battlefield like new.","oracle_id":"19ea326f-45ff-4bc0-a957-7d3f22dd8c6f","published_at":"2005-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose one opposing player as this card enters, and it only affects that one player. This choice is not changed even if this card changes controllers. It becomes useless but stays on the battlefield if the chosen player leaves the game.","oracle_id":"3d873e1d-4fac-42c4-bb31-77e76099e1ef","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The effect of lowering the maximum hand size makes it so the player discards down to 4 cards (instead of the usual 7) during the cleanup step.","oracle_id":"4f04603f-8f91-405b-b6ac-d2b66f05e32f","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose one opposing player just as this card is entering and it only affects that one player. This choice is not changed even if this card changes controllers. It becomes useless but stays on the battlefield if the chosen player leaves the game.","oracle_id":"4f04603f-8f91-405b-b6ac-d2b66f05e32f","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects modify your hand size, apply them in timestamp order. For example, if you put Null Profusion (an enchantment that says your maximum hand size is two) onto the battlefield and then a player puts Cursed Rack onto the battlefield choosing you, your maximum hand size will be four. However, if those permanents entered in the opposite order, your maximum hand size would be two.","oracle_id":"4f04603f-8f91-405b-b6ac-d2b66f05e32f","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Countering a spell that has been cast will not prevent you from drawing the card.","oracle_id":"7077ee9a-59c6-4b8e-bf33-9b094412ad38","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The triggered ability will trigger when you play a land card or cast a nonland card as a spell. It won't trigger when you play a copy of a card, such as with Isochron Scepter.","oracle_id":"7077ee9a-59c6-4b8e-bf33-9b094412ad38","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Your maximum hand size is checked only during the cleanup step of your turn. At any other time, you may have any number of cards in hand.","oracle_id":"7077ee9a-59c6-4b8e-bf33-9b094412ad38","published_at":"2007-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple effects modify your hand size, apply them in timestamp order. For example, if you put Spellbook (an artifact that says you have no maximum hand size) onto the battlefield and then put Null Profusion onto the battlefield, your maximum hand size will be two. However, if those permanents entered in the opposite order, you would have no maximum hand size.","oracle_id":"7077ee9a-59c6-4b8e-bf33-9b094412ad38","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You choose one opposing player as it enters and it only affects that one player. This choice is not changed even if Black Vise changes controllers. It becomes useless but stays on the battlefield if that player leaves the game.","oracle_id":"de7839fb-7040-48ab-a6d4-d1952972943d","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the chosen player has four or fewer cards in their hand as Black Vise's ability resolves, the ability just won't do anything that turn.","oracle_id":"de7839fb-7040-48ab-a6d4-d1952972943d","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
